WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.060
Configuration drift occurs when systems gradually deviate from approved baselines.

2
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:13.640
Drift may result from emergency changes, manual modifications, inconsistent deployments, undocumented updates, or tool failures.

3
00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:21.920
Over time, drift can create security weaknesses, operational instability, troubleshooting challenges, and compliance concerns.

4
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.660
A system may look familiar while no longer matching the approved configuration.

5
00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:30.460
Drift is especially risky when teams do not know it is happening.

6
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:36.880
Unknown differences make it harder to predict behavior, investigate issues, or confirm that required controls are operating.

7
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:41.240
Monitoring and periodic review help teams identify drift early.

8
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:49.740
The goal is to compare actual configurations against expected states and decide whether deviations should be corrected, approved, or investigated.
